sections.text:
A central bank is the main bank of a country. Examples are the Central Bank of Nigeria, Bank of Ghana, Central Bank of Kenya, South African Reserve Bank and Bank of England. Its usual functions are to:
issue or control the national currency;
act as banker to government and to commercial banks;
lend to banks in difficulty, as lender of last resort;
set monetary policy, for example through interest rates;
manage foreign reserves.

Most also supervise banks, or share this work with another body. Rules differ by country. Many countries also protect small deposits if a bank fails, as NDIC does in Nigeria.

Central bank na the main bank of one country. Examples na the Central Bank of Nigeria, Bank of Ghana, Central Bank of Kenya, South African Reserve Bank and Bank of England. Im usual functions na to:
issue or control the national currency;
act as banker to government and to commercial banks;
lend to banks wey dey for trouble, as lender of last resort (the last place banks fit borrow);
set monetary policy (how dem dey control money and credit for the country), for example through interest rates;
manage foreign reserves.

Most of them dey also supervise banks, or dem dey share this work with another body. Rules different by country. Many countries dey also protect small deposits if bank fail, as NDIC dey do for Nigeria.

Une banque centrale est la banque principale d’un pays. On peut citer la Central Bank of Nigeria, la Bank of Ghana, la Central Bank of Kenya, la South African Reserve Bank et la Banque d’Angleterre (Bank of England). Ses fonctions habituelles sont de :
émettre ou contrôler la monnaie nationale ;
servir de banque à l’État et aux banques commerciales ;
prêter aux banques en difficulté, en tant que prêteur en dernier ressort ;
fixer la politique monétaire, par exemple au moyen des taux d’intérêt ;
gérer les réserves de change.

La plupart contrôlent aussi les banques, ou partagent ce travail avec un autre organisme. Les règles diffèrent selon les pays. Beaucoup de pays protègent aussi les petits dépôts si une banque fait faillite, comme le fait la NDIC au Nigeria.

Benki kuu (central bank) ni benki mama, yaani benki kuu kabisa ya nchi. Mifano ni Benki Kuu ya Nigeria (Central Bank of Nigeria), Bank of Ghana, Benki Kuu ya Kenya (Central Bank of Kenya), South African Reserve Bank na Bank of England. Kazi zake za kawaida ni:
kutoa au kudhibiti sarafu ya taifa;
kuwa benki ya serikali na ya benki za biashara;
kukopesha benki zilizo katika matatizo, kama mkopeshaji wa mwisho (lender of last resort);
kuweka sera ya fedha (monetary policy), kwa mfano kupitia viwango vya riba;
kusimamia akiba ya fedha za kigeni (foreign reserves).

Nyingi pia husimamia benki, au hushirikiana kazi hii na chombo kingine. Kanuni hutofautiana kati ya nchi. Nchi nyingi pia hulinda amana ndogo benki ikifilisika, kama NDIC inavyofanya nchini Nigeria.

Um banco central (central bank) é o principal banco de um país. São exemplos o Central Bank of Nigeria, o Bank of Ghana, o Central Bank of Kenya, o South African Reserve Bank e o Bank of England. As suas funções habituais são:
emitir ou controlar a moeda nacional;
ser o banco do governo e dos bancos comerciais;
emprestar aos bancos em dificuldade, como prestamista de última instância (lender of last resort);
definir a política monetária, por exemplo através das taxas de juro;
gerir as reservas em moeda estrangeira.

A maioria também supervisiona os bancos, ou partilha este trabalho com outro organismo. As regras variam de país para país. Muitos países protegem também os pequenos depósitos se um banco falir, como faz a NDIC na Nigéria.

Un banco central (central bank) es el banco principal de un país. Son ejemplos el Central Bank of Nigeria, el Bank of Ghana, el Central Bank of Kenya, el South African Reserve Bank y el Banco de Inglaterra. Sus funciones habituales son:
emitir o controlar la moneda nacional;
actuar como banco del gobierno y de los bancos comerciales;
prestar a los bancos en dificultades, como prestamista de última instancia (lender of last resort);
fijar la política monetaria, por ejemplo mediante los tipos de interés;
gestionar las reservas de divisas.

La mayoría también supervisan a los bancos, o comparten este trabajo con otro organismo. Las normas varían según el país. Muchos países también protegen los depósitos pequeños si un banco quiebra, como hace la NDIC en Nigeria.
